Z||000000||86GT-FstBk||07-13-2000||08:18 PM||||My 2.8L V6 has 257,000 miles on it and has been rebuit twice.  I think it is time to put it down for good.  I want to keep it stock.  How hard would it be and how much would it cost to drop in another 2.8L V6.<P>TIA  Brian||||reg||5
Z||000001||Old Lar||07-13-2000||09:10 PM||||You've got lots of options.  A new 2.8, a remanufactured 2.8, a used 2.8.  Its all in the $$.  You can go to a 3.1, 3.4 same senerio as above.  The 3.1 and 3.4 are the easiest to swap out.  Professionally done a 3.4 installed is $4K.  The others are cheaper.  A remanufactures 3.1 is about $2K + installation.  The 3.1 and 3.4 done right will look just like a 2.8.  The innards are improved.  Used engines depending on milage can be gotten at Ed Parks Fiero Factory in Toney Alabama.  Ed has engines on site and could if there are no hitches, drop one in in a couple of days.  If you are a talented mechanic and have the time and tools and place to do it, you too could swap one out.  <P>I'm sure Ft. Benning has a great motor pool or auto shop on base where a swap could be done. <P>It all depends on $$ for what engine you get.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Linx||07-13-2000||09:14 PM||||I priced a rebuilt 2.8 from Jasper Engines, at $1600.  The whole engine.  Has a 3 yr 15k warrenty on it.  hard to beat that.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Black88GT||07-13-2000||09:43 PM||||If you want to keep it "stock", just do a 3.2L.  Bore it out .030 and use a 3.1 crank.  The 2.8 sucks.<P>||||reg||7
Z||000004||ThatRickGuy||07-14-2000||09:00 AM||||I'm doing exactly what BlackGT suggested, I pulled the 2.8 and stripped it down myself, it's going into the shop to get over bored, stroked, balances, and everything else. cost will be about $1400.||||reg||1
